{"abstract":"This one day workshop will explore queering as a design technique for troubling data and AI systems, ranging from quotidian personal data to recent Generative AI tools. By surfacing numerous instances of queering data or AI, we will come together to develop an archive of techniques for queering or artful subversion. From this archive, participants will select a technique and develop a speculative prototype or artifact via critical making. In doing so, we resist techno-determinism and conventional narratives of AI harms and benefits by tracing queer possibilities outside these categories.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Tran, Anh-Ton","Rothschild, Annabel","Kender, Kay","Osipova, Ekat","Kinnee, Brian","Taylor, Jordan","Meyer, Louie Søs","Haimson, Oliver L.","Light, Ann","DiSalvo, Carl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776427"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University","Georgia Institute of Technology","Malmö University","University of Michigan","University of Sussex","University of Washington","Vienna University of Technology"],"keyword":["Algorithmic Systems","Data","Design","Machine learning","Queering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"making trouble techniques for queering data and ai systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3658393","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776427","identifier":[{"id":"85198903258","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-97c4f392-7741-460d-bb14-56da8e6849b9"],"key